{"title":"Emergency Technologist Roadmap","role":"Emergency Technologist","summary":"An Emergency Technologist supports emergency and critical-care teams in the rapid assessment, stabilization, monitoring, and management of patients with acute medical or traumatic conditions.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Critical Care Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Emergency Technologist supports emergency and critical-care teams in the rapid assessment, stabilization, monitoring, and management of patients with acute medical or traumatic conditions."},{"type":"p","text":"The role typically involves working alongside emergency physicians, nurses, intensivists, paramedics, and other healthcare professionals in emergency departments, trauma centres, ICUs, and critical-care units."},{"type":"p","text":"Key responsibilities may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Emergency patient preparation and monitoring"},{"text":"Supporting resuscitation and emergency procedures"},{"text":"ECG and vital-sign monitoring"},{"text":"Maintaining emergency equipment and supplies"},{"text":"Assisting with airway and respiratory-support procedures under supervision"},{"text":"Supporting trauma and critical-care workflows"},{"text":"Collecting and documenting clinical observations"},{"text":"Infection-control and patient-safety practices"},{"text":"Preparing patients for diagnostic procedures and transfers"},{"text":"Maintaining accurate emergency-care documentation"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Exact scope of practice varies by institution, qualification, state, and applicable healthcare regulations. Clinical procedures should be performed only within the professional's authorized scope and under appropriate supervision."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Caree